# — so making the prelude unconditional cleared the whole manifest at once. The
# self-healing gate is what reported it: every one came back as UNEXPECTED PASS.
#
# One claim in the old manifest was simply wrong and is worth recording, because
# it mis-scoped four of the eight. It said `Cons`/`Nil` "was REMOVED from the
# language (Sprout lists are Vec / [...])" and that those fixtures "need
# rewriting, not just an import". They did not: `Cons`/`Nil` are the prelude's
# List constructors (stdlib/prelude.sprout:32-34) and always were. Nothing needed
# rewriting; they needed the prelude.
